      "text": "A transistor realization of the last circuit is shown in this slide. Two transistors M1 and M2 are used to realize the operational amplifier. A pMOST is used as a second stage to provide downwards level shifting. The expressions are exactly as before. The closed-loop gains A and v1 A are exactly the same as v2 before. Now the gain A of the 0 opamp has to be substituted by the gains of the two transistors. Each transistor provides a gain g r , as indicated. The loop gain LG depends on m o both gains. The input-and output-resistances are as before."
